# Mintlify publishes EVERY .md under this content root, whether or not it is in
# docs.json navigation. A page absent from the sidebar is still reachable by
# direct URL. "Not in the navigation" is not a privacy boundary — this file is.
#
# Internal documentation lives in the sibling `docs-internal/` root, which
# Mintlify never sees. These patterns are the second line of defence: if
# internal content lands here by mistake, it must not publish.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore syntax. See https://mintlify.com/docs/organize/mintignore

# Internal trees — must never exist under docs/, and must never publish if they do
next/
superpowers/
security/
drafts/
wip-docs/

# Incident write-ups and in-flight proposals belong in docs-internal/architecture/
architecture/incident-*.md
**/*-proposal.md

# Explicit opt-out marker for a single file
**/*.internal.md
**/*.internal.mdx

# Agent-tool variants of public pages (e.g. known-issues.claude.md).
# Mintlify auto-ignores the `.claude` DIRECTORY, not a `.claude.md` FILE.
**/*.claude.md
**/*.codex.md
**/*.agent.md
